# Square shapes only (no round)

AgainERP admin UI uses a squared visual language. Do not introduce rounded corners, pills, or circular chips.

Part of global UI rules — see `docs/ERP-UI-COMMON.md` and `.cursor/rules/erp-ui-common.mdc`.

## Required

- Prefer `rounded-none` on buttons, inputs, selects, cards, tables, dialogs, sheets, badges, and chips
- Status / role labels: squared borders (`border border-border`), not `rounded-full` pills
- Avatars / status dots: use squares (`rounded-none`), not circles
- Override shared primitives when needed: e.g. `Badge` → `className="rounded-none"`; icon buttons → `rounded-none`

## Forbidden

- `rounded-full`, `rounded-xl`, `rounded-lg`, `rounded-md`, `rounded-sm` on new or edited admin UI
- Pill-shaped filters, tags, or status toggles
- Soft “card” radius on list/table wrappers

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button className="rounded-full px-3 py-1">Active</button>
<div className="rounded-lg border">…</div>

// ✅ GOOD
<button className="rounded-none border border-border px-2 py-0.5">Active</button>
<div className="rounded-none border border-border">…</div>
```

Exception: only keep radius if an upstream library forces it and cannot be overridden — then neutralize with `[&_*]:rounded-none` / theme overrides where practical.
